{"Blacklist enforcement can be bypassed with case variants because `blacklistedGuestEmails` is lowercased but `guest` is not. Guest emails should be normalized before checking and persisting.": 0.9777956008911133, "The team permission check uses `&&` between `isTeamAdmin` and `isTeamOwner`, which only allows users who are both admin and owner, blocking normal admins from adding guests. Should use `||` if either role should grant access.": 0.9576689004898071, "`sendAddGuestsEmails` is called with the raw `guests` input instead of `uniqueGuests`, so existing attendees or blacklisted emails will still be treated as new guests in the email logic.": 0.9773797392845154, "`uniqueGuests` only excludes existing attendees/blacklist but does not dedupe duplicates within the `guests` input. If the same email appears twice, `createMany` can create duplicate attendee rows or hit a unique constraint.": 0.961083173751831, "Error code may display 'undefined' when `err.data.code` is not available, and the `unable_to_add_guests` fallback may not trigger correctly.": 0.874487042427063}